From: MoveCertificate contributors
Subject: [PATCH] kbase: import gralloc buffers GPU-uncached to avoid
 shareability faults

A/B experiment on the GPU_SHAREABILITY_FAULT: forcing
BASE_MEM_UNCACHED_GPU on every imported dma-buf makes the fault disappear
under a lock/unlock + notification-shade stress that otherwise fails in
4-8 seconds.  Imported buffers are cacheable CPU memory (CACHED_CPU in
the kernel's out.flags) and cached GPU transactions on those pages
conflict with their page-table shareability.  The backend already does
explicit MEM_SYNC cache maintenance, so GPU-uncached imports are safe.

--- a/src/panfrost/lib/kmod/kbase_kmod.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/lib/kmod/kbase_kmod.c
@@ -1886,10 +1886,21 @@ kbase_kmod_import_dmabuf(struct pan_kmod_dev *dev,
     * performs explicit cache maintenance (is_io_coherent == false), so the
     * coherent-system hint is not needed.
     */
+   /* kbase maps imported gralloc buffers as cacheable CPU memory
+    * (BASE_MEM_CACHED_CPU in out.flags).  Requesting cached GPU access for
+    * such shared buffers makes the GPU transactions' shareability disagree
+    * with the page-table attributes of the imported memory and the Mali MMU
+    * raises GPU_SHAREABILITY_FAULT (observed with ColorOS system buffers
+    * under HWUI/Vulkan: SystemUI dies a few seconds after a lock/unlock).
+    * Force GPU-uncached imports by default; CPU cache maintenance is still
+    * explicit through KBASE_IOCTL_MEM_SYNC.  Debug builds can still clear
+    * this bit via PANVK_KBASE_IMPORT_CLEAR /
+    * debug.panvk.kbase.import_clear for A/B runs.
+    */
    uint64_t import_flags =
       BASE_MEM_PROT_CPU_RD | BASE_MEM_PROT_CPU_WR |
       BASE_MEM_PROT_GPU_RD | BASE_MEM_PROT_GPU_WR |
-      BASE_MEM_IMPORT_SHARED;
+      BASE_MEM_IMPORT_SHARED | BASE_MEM_UNCACHED_GPU;
 
    if (kmod_flags & PAN_KMOD_BO_FLAG_GPU_UNCACHED)
       import_flags |= BASE_MEM_UNCACHED_GPU;
